This may not be what you're thinking of, but...

When two words are combined to make a new word that takes meaning from
both words, it's called a "portmanteau" word.  The classic example is
"slithy" from Lewis Carroll's "Jabberwocky" -- it's a portmanteau of
"lithe" and "slimy."  "Smog" and "brunch" are two more examples.

